// WHATWG Streams — pure-JS bootstrap.
//
// Covers the surface most consumers reach for: ReadableStream +
// default reader, WritableStream + default writer, TransformStream,
// pipeTo / pipeThrough, async iteration over a ReadableStream.
//
// Deliberately simpler than the spec reference implementation:
//   - No BYOB readers (no zero-copy byte streams yet)
//   - QueuingStrategy.highWaterMark is honored (queue length / size
//     accounting), but per-chunk size() callbacks fall back to 1
//   - tee() omitted for now (uncommon for app code; can be added if
//     a consumer needs it)
//   - Single-reader / single-writer locking enforced; teeing would
//     need a more elaborate state machine
//
// Bundle: this is the largest of the web-globals bootstraps (~50KB
// of source). Registered via its own `zjs_install_web_streams` so
// an embedder can selectively skip it for a tinier engine — the
// other Tier-2 web globals stay regardless.

